{title: Return To Sender}
{artist: Elvis Presley}
{key: C}
{# Источник: ручной перенос с UG. }

{comment: Intro}
[C]Return to [Am]sender, [Dm]return to [G7]sender

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]I gave a letter to the [Am]postman,
[Dm]he put it in his [G7]sack.
[C]Bright and early next [Am]morning,
he [Dm]brought my [G7]letter [C]back.

{comment: Chorus}
She wrote upon it:
[F]Return to [G7]sender, [F]address un[G7]known.
[F]No such [G7]number, [C]no such [C7]zone.
[F]We had a [G7]quarrel, [F]a lover's [G7]spat
[D7]I write I'm sorry but my [D]letter keeps [D7]coming [G7]back.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]So then I dropped it in the [Am]mailbox
[Dm]And sent it special [G7]D.
[C]Bright and early next [Am]morning
it [Dm]came right [G7]back to [C]me.

{comment: Chorus}
She wrote upon it:
[F]Return to [G7]sender, [F]address un[G7]known.
[F]No such [G7]person, [C]no such [C7]zone.

{comment: Bridge}
[F]This time I'm gonna take it myself
and [C]put it right in her hand.
And [D7]if it comes back the very next day
[G7]then I'll understand the writing on [G]it

{comment: Chorus}
[F]Return to [G7]sender, [F]address un[G7]known.
[F]No such [G7]number, [C]no such [C7]zone.

{comment: Outro}
[F]Return to [G7]sender (x3)
